From: arch-m4 project
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: apple: expose T6040 fixed-host role switch

The maintained T6040 fixed-host branch starts xHCI then returns before
registering its role provider. PD connector graph lookup therefore sees no
provider and returns -EPROBE_DEFER. Register the provider after successful
fixed-host initialization, outside the initialization lock. Preserve existing
host-only device-role rejection and unwind core initialization on registration
failure. Other fixed-host boards retain their original behavior.

Source-level candidate, built but not installed or loaded. PD IRQ/mux and
hotplug behavior still need native qualification on a separate boot.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -534,10 +534,23 @@
 		 * to reset the unused gadget side of the controller.
 		 */
 		appledwc->dwc.current_dr_role = DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST;
-		guard(mutex)(&appledwc->lock);
-		ret = dwc3_apple_init(appledwc, DWC3_APPLE_HOST);
+		{
+			guard(mutex)(&appledwc->lock);
+			ret = dwc3_apple_init(appledwc, DWC3_APPLE_HOST);
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to start fixed host controller\n");
+		/* T6040 PD connectors still consume a role switch in host mode. */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t6040")) {
+			ret = dwc3_apple_setup_role_switch(appledwc);
+			if (ret) {
+				guard(mutex)(&appledwc->lock);
+				dwc3_apple_exit(appledwc);
+				dwc3_core_remove(&appledwc->dwc);
+				return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+						     "Failed to setup fixed-host role switch\n");
+			}
+		}
 		return 0;
 	}
 
